.th NEQN I 5/31/77
.sh NAME
neqn \*- typeset mathematics on terminal
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd neqn
[ file ] ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Neqn
is an
.it nroff\^\c
(I)
preprocessor.
The input language is the same as that of
.it eqn\^\c
(I).
Normal usage is almost always:
.s3
	neqn file ... | nroff
.s3
Output is meant for terminals with
forward and reverse capabilities, such as
the
.if n \%TELETYPE(Rg.)
.if t \%\s-2TELETYPE\s+2\(rg
Model 37
or GSI (DASI or DIABLO) terminals.
.s3
If no arguments are specified,
.it neqn
reads the standard input,
so it may be used as a filter.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
eqn(I), gsi(I), mm(I),
DASI450(VII), GSI300(VII)
.br
.it "Typesetting Mathematics \\- User's Guide (2nd Edition)"
by B. W. Kernighan and L. L. Cherry.
.br
.it "New Graphic Symbols for EQN and NEQN"
by C. Scrocca.
.sh BUGS
Because of some interactions with 
.it nroff\^\c
(I),
there may not always be enough space left before and after
lines containing equations.
